{
  "issue": 4,
  "title": "Add a `limit` argument to search()",
  "summary": "Add an optional limit to searches on the default table and named tables. Limited searches return the first matching documents in the existing search order, while unlimited searches and query caching preserve their existing results.",
  "issue_type": "feature",
  "source_excerpts": [
    {
      "id": "SRC-1",
      "quote": "Could `search` take an optional `limit`?"
    },
    {
      "id": "SRC-2",
      "quote": "`limit=N` returns at most N documents, the first N matches in the normal order (document id / insertion order), same order `search` already uses"
    },
    {
      "id": "SRC-3",
      "quote": "`limit=None` (the default) means no limit, so existing code doesn't change"
    },
    {
      "id": "SRC-4",
      "quote": "if there are fewer matches than `limit`, just return all of them"
    },
    {
      "id": "SRC-5",
      "quote": "should work on `db.table('x').search(...)` too, not just the default table"
    },
    {
      "id": "SRC-6",
      "quote": "I don't want `search(q, limit=1)` followed by `search(q)` to suddenly give me only 1 result (or the other way round)"
    },
    {
      "id": "SRC-7",
      "quote": "a negative `limit` (e.g. `limit=-1`) should raise `ValueError`. `limit=0` returns an empty list."
    }
  ],
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "REQ-1",
      "text": "Searches on the default table and named tables shall accept an optional limit that returns at most that many matching documents in the existing search order.",
      "provenance": "STATED",
      "sources": ["SRC-1", "SRC-2", "SRC-4", "SRC-5"]
    },
    {
      "id": "REQ-2",
      "text": "A search with the limit omitted or set to None shall return all matches in the existing search order.",
      "provenance": "STATED",
      "sources": ["SRC-3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "REQ-3",
      "text": "A search with a negative limit shall raise ValueError, and a search with limit zero shall return an empty list.",
      "provenance": "CONFIRMED",
      "sources": ["SRC-7"]
    },
    {
      "id": "REQ-4",
      "text": "A search shall return the results specified by its own limit regardless of whether a previous search for the same query used a different limit.",
      "provenance": "STATED",
      "sources": ["SRC-6"]
    }
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC-1",
      "requirement": "REQ-1",
      "given": "A TinyDB using MemoryStorage whose default table contains, in insertion order, {'status': 'open', 'n': 1}, {'status': 'closed', 'n': 2}, {'status': 'open', 'n': 3}, and {'status': 'open', 'n': 4}; q is Query().status == 'open'.",
      "when": "Call db.search(q, limit=2).",
      "then": "The first two matching documents are returned in insertion order.",
      "observable": "The returned list equals [{'status': 'open', 'n': 1}, {'status': 'open', 'n': 3}]."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-2",
      "requirement": "REQ-1",
      "given": "A TinyDB using MemoryStorage whose named table 'x' contains, in insertion order, {'n': 1} and {'n': 2}; q is Query().n > 0.",
      "when": "Call db.table('x').search(q, limit=5).",
      "then": "Both matching documents are returned in insertion order.",
      "observable": "The returned list equals [{'n': 1}, {'n': 2}]."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-3",
      "requirement": "REQ-2",
      "given": "A TinyDB using MemoryStorage whose default table contains, in insertion order, {'n': 1} and {'n': 2}; q is Query().n > 0.",
      "when": "Call db.search(q, limit=None).",
      "then": "Both matching documents are returned in insertion order.",
      "observable": "The returned list equals [{'n': 1}, {'n': 2}]."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-4",
      "requirement": "REQ-3",
      "given": "A TinyDB using MemoryStorage whose default table contains {'n': 1}; q is Query().n > 0.",
      "when": "Call db.search(q, limit=0).",
      "then": "The search returns no documents.",
      "observable": "The returned value equals []."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-5",
      "requirement": "REQ-3",
      "given": "A TinyDB using MemoryStorage whose default table contains {'n': 1}; q is Query().n > 0.",
      "when": "Call db.search(q, limit=-1).",
      "then": "The search rejects the negative limit.",
      "observable": "The call raises ValueError."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-6",
      "requirement": "REQ-4",
      "given": "A TinyDB using MemoryStorage with the default query cache enabled; its default table contains, in insertion order, {'n': 1} and {'n': 2}; q is Query().n > 0; db.search(q, limit=1) has already been called.",
      "when": "Call db.search(q).",
      "then": "The unlimited search returns both matching documents in insertion order.",
      "observable": "The returned list equals [{'n': 1}, {'n': 2}]."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-7",
      "requirement": "REQ-4",
      "given": "A TinyDB using MemoryStorage with the default query cache enabled; its default table contains, in insertion order, {'n': 1} and {'n': 2}; q is Query().n > 0; db.search(q) has already been called.",
      "when": "Call db.search(q, limit=1).",
      "then": "The limited search returns only the first matching document.",
      "observable": "The returned list equals [{'n': 1}]."
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [],
  "out_of_scope": [
    "Changes to ordering or sorting beyond preserving the existing search order.",
    "Behavior for limit values other than None and integers is not specified by the issue."
  ],
  "injection_findings": [],
  "spec_md": "# Issue 4: Add a `limit` argument to search()\n\n**Status: READY** — no blocking questions.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd an optional search limit for the default table and named tables. Results retain the existing search order, and a previous search with a different limit must not change a later search's results.\n\n## Sources\n\n- SRC-1: “Could `search` take an optional `limit`?”\n- SRC-2: “`limit=N` returns at most N documents, the first N matches in the normal order (document id / insertion order), same order `search` already uses”\n- SRC-3: “`limit=None` (the default) means no limit, so existing code doesn't change”\n- SRC-4: “if there are fewer matches than `limit`, just return all of them”\n- SRC-5: “should work on `db.table('x').search(...)` too, not just the default table”\n- SRC-6: “I don't want `search(q, limit=1)` followed by `search(q)` to suddenly give me only 1 result (or the other way round)”\n- SRC-7: “a negative `limit` (e.g. `limit=-1`) should raise `ValueError`. `limit=0` returns an empty list.”\n\n## Requirements\n\n- REQ-1 (STATED; SRC-1, SRC-2, SRC-4, SRC-5): Searches on the default table and named tables shall accept an optional limit that returns at most that many matching documents in the existing search order.\n- REQ-2 (STATED; SRC-3): A search with the limit omitted or set to None shall return all matches in the existing search order.\n- REQ-3 (CONFIRMED; SRC-7): A search with a negative limit shall raise ValueError, and a search with limit zero shall return an empty list.\n- REQ-4 (STATED; SRC-6): A search shall return the results specified by its own limit regardless of whether a previous search for the same query used a different limit.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- AC-1 (REQ-1): Given a MemoryStorage database with default-table documents {'status': 'open', 'n': 1}, {'status': 'closed', 'n': 2}, {'status': 'open', 'n': 3}, and {'status': 'open', 'n': 4}, in that order, and q = Query().status == 'open', when db.search(q, limit=2) is called, then it returns [{'status': 'open', 'n': 1}, {'status': 'open', 'n': 3}].\n- AC-2 (REQ-1): Given a MemoryStorage database with named table 'x' containing {'n': 1} and {'n': 2}, in that order, and q = Query().n > 0, when db.table('x').search(q, limit=5) is called, then it returns [{'n': 1}, {'n': 2}].\n- AC-3 (REQ-2): Given a MemoryStorage database with default-table documents {'n': 1} and {'n': 2}, in that order, and q = Query().n > 0, when db.search(q, limit=None) is called, then it returns [{'n': 1}, {'n': 2}].\n- AC-4 (REQ-3): Given a MemoryStorage database with default-table document {'n': 1} and q = Query().n > 0, when db.search(q, limit=0) is called, then it returns [].\n- AC-5 (REQ-3): Given a MemoryStorage database with default-table document {'n': 1} and q = Query().n > 0, when db.search(q, limit=-1) is called, then it raises ValueError.\n- AC-6 (REQ-4): Given a MemoryStorage database with the default query cache enabled, default-table documents {'n': 1} and {'n': 2} in that order, q = Query().n > 0, and a prior call to db.search(q, limit=1), when db.search(q) is called, then it returns [{'n': 1}, {'n': 2}].\n- AC-7 (REQ-4): Given a MemoryStorage database with the default query cache enabled, default-table documents {'n': 1} and {'n': 2} in that order, q = Query().n > 0, and a prior call to db.search(q), when db.search(q, limit=1) is called, then it returns [{'n': 1}].\n\n## Open questions and assumptions\n\nNone.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nChanges to sorting beyond preserving existing search order; behavior for limit values other than None and integers is unspecified.\n\n## Injection findings\n\nNone."
}
